@startuml readme-topology
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: the README's how-it-works diagram (readme-topology.svg) and how the README's hero.gif is made
' covers: README.md
' covers: _spec/_assets/hero.gif
' covers: _spec/_assets/readme-topology.svg
'
' ── RENDER (DECIDED 2026-11-17) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
' GitHub renders no PlantUML, so the README embeds this file's SVG:
'   mise x conda:plantuml@1.2026.10 -- plantuml -tsvg _spec/_assets/readme-topology.puml
' NOT CHOSEN: Mermaid (a second diagram language beside every spec); ASCII
' boxes (static, and unlike the spec look).
' The shape follows the run form's topology strip
' (_spec/internal/choiceui/topology-strip.puml): host → sbx microVM → sbx proxy → cloud.
'
' ── THE HERO GIF (RECORDED 2026-11-18) ──────────────────────────────────────
' A detached tmux at 112×34 types `proveo claudecode` in a Git copy of e2e/samples
' named acme. It selects apps/api in the scope picker, confirms the run, and
' holds the live Claude Code input prompt for about five seconds before looping.
' Use PS1='$ ', TERM=xterm-256color, COLORTERM=truecolor, PROVEO_WIZARD=on,
' PROVEO_AGENT_UPDATE=0, PROVEO_GLYPHS=safe and fresh Proveo home and state dirs.
' The recording host lacked KVM. A recording-only adapter passes the launch
' arguments to Claude Code 2.1.322 in proveo/claudecode:latest using Docker.
' The container has networking disabled and uses a fixture config and credential.
' Capture changed frames with `tmux capture-pane -e -p`, cursor position and time.
' Render ANSI cells with pyte and Pillow using DejaVu Sans Mono and Noto Sans
' Symbols 2. Export the frames with ffmpeg at 12 fps and a 256-color palette.
' HISTORY: the earlier recording ended in the devices picker.

left to right direction
skinparam nodesep 40
skinparam ranksep 60

actor "you" as You
node "host · macOS · Linux" as Host <<host>> {
  component "**proveo**\nrun form · sbx Kit · .env" as CLI <<app>>
  database "~~/.proveo\nsessions · toolchains" as Home <<db>>
  component "Ollama · Chrome\nopt-in host services" as HostSvc <<app>>
}
node "sbx microVM" as VM <<host>> {
  component "**agent**\nclaudecode · codex · cursor\nopencode · hermes" as Agent <<app>>
  database "repo clone\nbrowser · android add-ons" as Clone <<db>>
}
component "**sbx proxy**\nholds your API keys" as Proxy <<async>>
cloud "LLM providers\nallowed domains" as Cloud <<cloud>>
database "your repo\nrefs/proveo/<sid>" as Repo <<db>>

You ARROW_MAIN CLI : proveo run <agent>
CLI ARROW_MAIN VM : sbx create · run
CLI ARROW_QUEUE Home : sessions persist
Agent ARROW_MAIN Clone : edits · commits
Agent ARROW_CLOUD Proxy : egress under sbx policy
Proxy ARROW_CLOUD Cloud : key attached
Agent ARROW_OPTIONAL HostSvc : host.docker.internal
Clone ARROW_MAIN Repo : teardown · proveo adopt
@enduml
